.TH std::seed_seq::param 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::seed_seq::param \- std::seed_seq::param

.SH Synopsis
template< class OutputIt >          \fI(since C++11)\fP
void param( OutputIt dest ) const;

Copies the stored seeds to the range beginning with dest. Equivalent to
std::copy(v ﻿.begin(),  v ﻿.end(), dest);.

If values of type result_type are not writable to dest, the program is ill-formed.

If OutputIt does not satisfy the requirements of LegacyOutputIterator, the behavior is
undefined.

.SH Parameters

dest - the beginning iterator of the output range

.SH Exceptions

Only throws the exceptions thrown by the operations on dest.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <iostream>
#include <iterator>
#include <random>

int main()
{
    std::seed_seq s1 = {-1, 0, 1};
    s1.param(std::ostream_iterator<int>(std::cout, " "));
}

.SH Output:

-1 0 1

